  array (
    'id' => 1,
    'title' => 'Complete Travel Guide to Chhatrapati Sambhajinagar in 2026',
    'content' => '<h2>Welcome to Chhatrapati Sambhajinagar (Aurangabad) ? Your Complete 2026 Travel Guide</h2>

<p>Chhatrapati Sambhajinagar, formerly known as Aurangabad, is Maharashtra\'s crown jewel of heritage tourism. Home to two UNESCO World Heritage Sites ? the Ajanta Caves and Ellora Caves ? this city draws over 1 million visitors every year. Whether you\'re a history buff, a spiritual seeker, or simply a curious traveller, this guide covers everything you need to plan the perfect trip in 2026.</p>

<h2>Top Attractions in Chhatrapati Sambhajinagar</h2>

<h3>1. Ajanta Caves ? UNESCO World Heritage Site</h3>
<p>Located 100 km from the city, the Ajanta Caves are a collection of 30 rock-cut Buddhist cave monuments dating from the 2nd century BCE to 480 CE. The caves feature extraordinary paintings and sculptures depicting the life of the Buddha. Entry fee: ?40 (Indians), ?600 (foreigners). Best visited between October and March.</p>

<h3>2. Ellora Caves ? Three Religions, One Marvel</h3>
<p>Just 30 km from the city, Ellora\'s 34 caves represent Buddhist, Hindu, and Jain traditions carved between the 6th and 11th centuries. The Kailasa Temple (Cave 16) is the world\'s largest monolithic rock excavation. Entry fee: ?40 (Indians), ?600 (foreigners). Open Tuesday to Sunday, 6 AM to 6 PM.</p>

<h3>3. Bibi Ka Maqbara ? The Taj of the Deccan</h3>
<p>Built in 1660 by Mughal prince Azam Shah in memory of his mother Dilras Banu Begum, Bibi Ka Maqbara is often called the "Taj of the Deccan." Located just 6 km from the city centre, it\'s a must-visit for architecture lovers. Entry fee: ?25 (Indians), ?300 (foreigners).</p>

<h3>4. Daulatabad Fort</h3>
<p>This 12th-century hilltop fortress, 15 km from the city, was once the capital of the Yadava dynasty. The fort features a unique conical hill, a moat, and a labyrinthine tunnel designed to confuse invaders. Climbing to the top rewards you with panoramic views of the Deccan plateau.</p>

<h3>5. Panchakki Water Mill</h3>
<p>A 17th-century marvel of engineering, Panchakki is a water mill powered by an underground channel. The complex includes a large garden, a fish-filled tank, and the dargah of Sufi saint Hazrat Shah Musafir. Entry fee: ?25.</p>

<h3>6. Grishneshwar Temple</h3>
<p>One of the 12 Jyotirlingas of Lord Shiva, Grishneshwar Temple is located near Ellora Caves. It\'s a significant pilgrimage site and a beautiful example of Hemadpanthi architecture. Entry is free.</p>

<h2>Best Time to Visit Chhatrapati Sambhajinagar</h2>

<p><strong>October to March</strong> is the ideal time to visit. The weather is pleasant with temperatures between 15?C and 28?C, perfect for sightseeing at outdoor monuments. Avoid May and June when temperatures can exceed 42?C.</p>

<ul>
<li><strong>October?November:</strong> Post-monsoon greenery, cool weather, fewer crowds</li>
<li><strong>December?January:</strong> Peak tourist season, best weather, book hotels in advance</li>
<li><strong>February?March:</strong> Warm but comfortable, Ellora Festival held in February</li>
<li><strong>July?September:</strong> Monsoon season ? Ajanta Caves look lush but roads can be slippery</li>
</ul>

<h2>How to Reach Chhatrapati Sambhajinagar</h2>

<h3>By Air</h3>
<p>Chhatrapati Sambhajinagar Airport (IXU) has direct flights from Mumbai, Delhi, Hyderabad, and Bengaluru. The airport is 10 km from the city centre. Taxis and auto-rickshaws are available outside.</p>

<h3>By Train</h3>
<p>Aurangabad Railway Station is well-connected to Mumbai (Tapovan Express, 7 hours), Pune (5 hours), and Hyderabad (6 hours). The Devagiri Express and Janshatabdi Express are popular options.</p>

<h3>By Road</h3>
<p>The city is 335 km from Mumbai (6 hours via NH52), 235 km from Pune (4.5 hours), and 500 km from Hyderabad (8 hours). MSRTC buses run regularly from all major Maharashtra cities.</p>

<h2>Where to Stay in Chhatrapati Sambhajinagar</h2>

<p>The city offers accommodation for every budget. From luxury hotels near the railway station to budget homestays in the old city, you\'ll find plenty of options. CSNExplore lists verified hotels, homestays, and service apartments with real photos and honest reviews.</p>

<ul>
<li><strong>Budget (?500??1,500/night):</strong> ITS HOME Home Stay Inn, Hotel Blossom</li>
<li><strong>Mid-range (?1,500??4,000/night):</strong> Treebo Aroma Executive, Hotel The Gravity Inn</li>
<li><strong>Luxury (?4,000+/night):</strong> Vivanta Aurangabad, Lemon Tree Hotel</li>
</ul>

<h2>Getting Around the City</h2>

<h3>Car Rental</h3>
<p>Renting a car is the most convenient way to cover Ajanta and Ellora in a single day. CSNExplore offers self-drive and chauffeur-driven options starting from ?800/day. Popular choices include Maruti Swift, Tata Punch, and Toyota Innova for groups.</p>

<h3>Bike Rental</h3>
<p>For solo travellers and couples, renting a bike or scooter is the most flexible option. Honda Activa and Hero Splendor rentals start from ?300/day. Explore the city at your own pace without worrying about parking.</p>

<h3>Auto-Rickshaw</h3>
<p>Auto-rickshaws are widely available and affordable for short distances within the city. Negotiate the fare before boarding or insist on the meter.</p>

<h2>Local Food & Cuisine</h2>

<p>Chhatrapati Sambhajinagar has a rich culinary tradition influenced by Mughal, Maratha, and Hyderabadi cuisines.</p>

<ul>
<li><strong>Naan Khaliya:</strong> Slow-cooked mutton curry served with naan bread ? a local specialty</li>
<li><strong>Tahri:</strong> Spiced rice cooked with vegetables, a popular street food</li>
<li><strong>Sheer Khurma:</strong> A rich vermicelli pudding made with milk, dates, and dry fruits</li>
<li><strong>Biryani:</strong> Aurangabadi biryani has a distinct flavour ? lighter than Hyderabadi but equally aromatic</li>
<li><strong>Misal Pav:</strong> A spicy sprouted lentil curry served with bread rolls</li>
</ul>

<h2>Shopping in Chhatrapati Sambhajinagar</h2>

<p>The city is famous for its traditional crafts. Don\'t leave without picking up:</p>

<ul>
<li><strong>Himroo Shawls:</strong> Handwoven silk-cotton fabric with intricate patterns, a 700-year-old tradition</li>
<li><strong>Paithani Sarees:</strong> Silk sarees with gold zari borders, a prized possession</li>
<li><strong>Bidriware:</strong> Black metal handicrafts inlaid with silver, originating from Bidar</li>
<li><strong>Leather Goods:</strong> The city has a long tradition of leather craftsmanship</li>
</ul>

<p>Best shopping areas: Gulmandi Market, Shahaganj, and the shops near Bibi Ka Maqbara.</p>

<h2>Travel Tips for 2026</h2>

<ul>
<li>Book Ajanta Caves tickets online in advance during peak season (December?January) to avoid long queues</li>
<li>Carry cash ? many local restaurants and auto-rickshaws don\'t accept cards</li>
<li>Wear comfortable walking shoes ? Ellora Caves involve significant walking on uneven terrain</li>
<li>Hire a licensed guide at Ajanta and Ellora for a richer experience (?500??800 for 2 hours)</li>
<li>Photography is allowed at most monuments but flash photography is prohibited inside the caves</li>
<li>The Ellora Festival (February) features classical music and dance performances at the cave backdrop ? highly recommended</li>
</ul>

<h2>Plan Your Trip with CSNExplore</h2>

<p>CSNExplore is Chhatrapati Sambhajinagar\'s dedicated travel platform. We offer verified hotel bookings, car and bike rentals, attraction guides, and restaurant recommendations ? all in one place. Call or WhatsApp us at +91-8600968888 for personalised trip planning assistance.</p>',
